168:This kind of auction is like a big gamble, and it's really exciting to try to push the limits of the price as far as possible. However, when the auctioneer calls out 7 million Coppers, I see someone in the front row raise their number plate. If I don't follow at this moment, it will mean I am giving up on this cut flower. After thinking for a moment, I decide to raise my number plate.
169:Three people raised their number plates in this round. According to the rules of the auction, we will now make increasing bids starting from 7 million Coppers, and each bid must be at least an increase of half a million Coppers.
170:Someone shouts out 7.5 million Coppers right after the auctioneer explains the rules. To follow suit, I and the buyer who raised their number plate first will have to raise the bid to 8 million Coppers.
171:8 million Coppers... I guess that's reasonable. In addition, I'll miss out on this flower directly if I give up now, so there is room for me to struggle.
172:After weighing my options, I call out the price of 8 million Coppers.
173:The crisp sound of the mallet announces my success. The two other buyers choose to give up.
