476:{character:player}(Text message) You make a lot of sense. I'm starting to get worried.
477:Unknown Number
478:Me
479:{character:Unknown Number}(Text message) I want to remind you that although everyone can bid on all three cut flower arrangements, each person can only win the bid for one of them.
480:{character:Unknown Number}(Text message) Yes.
481:{character:Unknown Number}(Text message) By the way, why is my number still appearing as an unknown number on your phone?
482:{character:Noah}(Text message) It's up to your own judgment. The boss asked me not to say too much to avoid interfering with your thinking.
483:{character:Noah}(Text message) But according to the information I just received, this year's flower arrangement looks superior to the ones sold in the last two years.
484:{character:Noah}(Text message) There are records of the price the coral red skimmia was sold for in the last two years. It was sold for 6.3 million Coppers and 7.1 million Coppers respectively in the last two years.
485:{character:player}(Text message) I thought the flowers are just symbolic and the real thing that people are bidding on is an afternoon tea.
486:{character:Noah}(Text message) The snow peonies in this flower arrangement that will be auctioned off soon are grown as a pair, and it's quite rare for them to grow to this size. According to Strix's information database, this is Countless Springs's latest flower breed, and this is the first time it is being sold in their auction.
487:{character:Noah}(Text message) The price the coral red skimmia was sold for in the last two years is available. It was sold for 6.3 million Coppers and 7.1 million Coppers respectively in the last two years. Its price has gone up by a lot this time.
489:Narration
490:Kutsuji
492:{character:Noah}(Text message) Although there are no historical selling prices for this cut flower arrangement, the boss will definitely estimate a price based on the selling prices of the two previous cut flower arrangements. If you paid way too much for the cut flower, given his personality, he would definitely find a way to make you compensate him for the extra amount.
493:The time displayed on my mobile phone is 6:06.
494:{character:Noah}(Text message) The flowing gold camellia sold for 6.5 million Coppers last year. The price increased by one million this year.
495:*Sigh*... I've been oversleeping lately, which makes me feel out of place in the busy One Han City.
